{% block body %}
    <div class="container">

        <h1>AC13.01 – Using a computer system and its tools</h1>

        <p>
            <strong>Objective :</strong>
            Install, configure, and use the tools required for software development.
        </p>

        <hr>

        <h2>Reflective analysis</h2>

        <p>
            In this activity, I learned how to use a complete development environment
            to work on software projects.
        </p>

        <p>
            I installed and configured essential tools such as Node.js, Git, and Visual Studio Code.
            These tools allow the creation, management, and execution of web projects.
        </p>

        <p>
            I used the terminal to execute various commands such as installing dependencies,
            initializing projects, and managing versions with Git.
        </p>

        <p>
            This activity helped me understand how a professional development workstation works
            and how development tools are organized in a real company environment.
        </p>

        <h2>Supporting documents</h2>
        <ul>
            <li>Installation of Node.js and Git</li>
            <li>Use of the terminal (npm, git)</li>
            <li>VS Code configuration</li>
            <li>Creation of a React project</li>
        </ul>

